Thetrystatement allows you to define a block of code to be 
tested for errors while it is being executed.

Thecatchstatement allows you to define a block of code to 
be executed, if an error occurs in the try block.

The JavaScript statementstryandcatchcome in pairs:

AReferenceErroroccurs if you use (reference) a variable that does not exist.

AType Erroroccurs when a value is of the wrong type or an operation
is invalid on that type.

ARangeErroroccurs when a value is out of its valid range.

AnURIErroroccurs if you use illegal characters in a URI function:

ASyntax Erroroccurs when the code violates JavaScript's grammar rules.

